  "reason": "The second design (IC50 ≈ 319 nM) was much better than the third, so I reverted to that general scaffold but optimized around features SHAP favored: multiple heteroatoms in rings, O–C–N linkages, and halogens, while avoiding disfavored C–N–C aliphatic motifs and overconjugated alkenes. I kept the dichloroaryl core and heteroaromatic amide, replaced the Michael acceptor with a non-conjugated amide, introduced an additional morpholine ring to add polar heteroatom-rich cycles, and slightly shortened the linker to reduce flexibility and metabolic vulnerability, aiming for higher potency and better fit to the model’s preferred fragments.",
